==============================================================================================
READING (Morse + band-barrier + Borsuk-Ulam)
==============================================================================================
 - L_C = super-level set {g_C>=1/14} = arcs around the LOCAL MAXIMA of the PL Morse function g_C;
   delta_max = widest 'hole'. Three-distance bounds the #slopes (=> structured arc widths for AP cores).
 - The far W carves with thin danger teeth (width 1/(7W)); a hole survives iff wider than a tooth
   (delta_max>1/(7W)). This IS the band-barrier: thin bands cannot cover fat holes.
 - L_C is ANTIPODE-SYMMETRIC (||v(-t)||=||vt|| => t in L_C <=> -t in L_C); the Z/2 (complement/iota)
   action is free off the fixed points {0,1/2}; whether a hole survives is the iota-odd (Borsuk-Ulam)
   index -- the topological packaging of the band-barrier (klein-S56 iota-odd = OPEN-Q-108 residual).
 - NET: single-far closes for small-max cores (fat holes, W*<=182 overlaps klein); large internal
   speeds (thin holes, W*>182) are the multi-far residual = >=2 large speeds = the r-far ladder.
DONE.
